CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result.',objectives=array['Represent the given information accurately in polynomials and quadratics.','Select and apply the appropriate formula or property in polynomials and quadratics.','Show an efficient solution without skipping essential reasoning in polynomials and quadratics.','Check magnitude, sign, units, and reasonableness in polynomials and quadratics.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Operate on polynomials and solve basic quadratic equations."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"For ab = 0, either a = 0 or b = 0."},{"title":"CET application","body":"CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Identify what is given and what must be found.','Rewrite the information using symbols, a table, or a labeled sketch.','Choose the property or formula that connects the known and unknown values.','Carry out one justified operation at a time and keep units consistent.','Substitute the result back or estimate to confirm that it is reasonable.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":null,"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 8x + 12?","answer":"(x - 2)(x - 6)","solution":"The factors need sum 8 and product 12; the roots are 2 and 6."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":null,"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 10x + 21?","answer":"(x - 3)(x - 7)","solution":"The factors need sum 10 and product 21; the roots are 3 and 7."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":null,"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 12x + 32?","answer":"(x - 4)(x - 8)","solution":"The factors need sum 12 and product 32; the roots are 4 and 8."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Starting computation before identifying the required quantity.','Applying a memorized formula to the wrong relationship.','Dropping a negative sign, unit, exponent, or grouping symbol.','Accepting an answer without checking it against the original conditions.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Estimate before solving so unreasonable options are easier to eliminate.','Write one clean intermediate line for multi-step calculations.','Use answer choices strategically, but still verify the governing method.','Return to skipped hard items after securing faster questions.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 14x + 45?","answer":"(x - 5)(x - 9)","explanation":"The factors need sum 14 and product 45; the roots are 5 and 9."},{"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 16x + 60?","answer":"(x - 6)(x - 10)","explanation":"The factors need sum 16 and product 60; the roots are 6 and 10."},{"prompt":"Which is the factored form of x² - 13x + 22?","answer":"(x - 2)(x - 11)","explanation":"The factors need sum 13 and product 22; the roots are 2 and 11."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='polynomials' and s.slug='mathematics';
