CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result.',objectives=array['Represent the given information accurately in functions and graphs.','Select and apply the appropriate formula or property in functions and graphs.','Show an efficient solution without skipping essential reasoning in functions and graphs.','Check magnitude, sign, units, and reasonableness in functions and graphs.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Read function notation, tables, and graphs."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"A function assigns each input exactly one output."},{"title":"CET application","body":"CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Identify what is given and what must be found.','Rewrite the information using symbols, a table, or a labeled sketch.','Choose the property or formula that connects the known and unknown values.','Carry out one justified operation at a time and keep units consistent.','Substitute the result back or estimate to confirm that it is reasonable.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":null,"prompt":"If f(x) = 2x + 3, what is f(1)?","answer":"5","solution":"Substitute 1: f(1) = 2(1) + 3 = 5."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":null,"prompt":"If f(x) = 3x + 4, what is f(2)?","answer":"10","solution":"Substitute 2: f(2) = 3(2) + 4 = 10."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":null,"prompt":"If f(x) = 4x + 5, what is f(3)?","answer":"17","solution":"Substitute 3: f(3) = 4(3) + 5 = 17."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Starting computation before identifying the required quantity.','Applying a memorized formula to the wrong relationship.','Dropping a negative sign, unit, exponent, or grouping symbol.','Accepting an answer without checking it against the original conditions.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Estimate before solving so unreasonable options are easier to eliminate.','Write one clean intermediate line for multi-step calculations.','Use answer choices strategically, but still verify the governing method.','Return to skipped hard items after securing faster questions.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"If f(x) = 5x + 6, what is f(4)?","answer":"26","explanation":"Substitute 4: f(4) = 5(4) + 6 = 26."},{"prompt":"If f(x) = 6x + 7, what is f(5)?","answer":"37","explanation":"Substitute 5: f(5) = 6(5) + 7 = 37."},{"prompt":"If f(x) = 7x + 3, what is f(6)?","answer":"45","explanation":"Substitute 6: f(6) = 7(6) + 3 = 45."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='functions' and s.slug='mathematics';
