What is term 7?","answer":"27","solution":"aₙ = a₁ + (n - 1)d = 3 + (7 - 1)(4) = 27."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Starting computation before identifying the required quantity.','Applying a memorized formula to the wrong relationship.','Dropping a negative sign, unit, exponent, or grouping symbol.','Accepting an answer without checking it against the original conditions.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Estimate before solving so unreasonable options are easier to eliminate.','Write one clean intermediate line for multi-step calculations.','Use answer choices strategically, but still verify the governing method.','Return to skipped hard items after securing faster questions.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"An arithmetic sequence begins with 4 and has common difference 5. What is term 8?","answer":"39","explanation":"aₙ = a₁ + (n - 1)d = 4 + (8 - 1)(5) = 39."},{"prompt":"An arithmetic sequence begins with 5 and has common difference 6. What is term 9?","answer":"53","explanation":"aₙ = a₁ + (n - 1)d = 5 + (9 - 1)(6) = 53."},{"prompt":"An arithmetic sequence begins with 6 and has common difference 7. What is term 5?","answer":"34","explanation":"aₙ = a₁ + (n - 1)d = 6 + (5 - 1)(7) = 34."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='sequences' and s.slug='mathematics';
update public.lessons l set overview='Summarize and interpret data displays. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result.',objectives=array['Represent the given information accurately in statistics and data interpretation.','Select and apply the appropriate formula or property in statistics and data interpretation.','Show an efficient solution without skipping essential reasoning in statistics and data interpretation.','Check magnitude, sign, units, and reasonableness in statistics and data interpretation.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Summarize and interpret data displays."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"The mean is sensitive to extreme values; the median is more resistant."},{"title":"CET application","body":"CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Identify what is given and what must be found.','Rewrite the information using symbols, a table, or a labeled sketch.','Choose the property or formula that connects the known and unknown values.','Carry out one justified operation at a time and keep units consistent.','Substitute the result back or estimate to confirm that it is reasonable.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":null,"prompt":"What is the median of 4, 6, 8, 10, 12?","answer":"8","solution":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 8."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":null,"prompt":"What is the median of 5, 8, 11, 14, 17?","answer":"11","solution":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 11."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":null,"prompt":"What is the median of 6, 10, 14, 18, 22?","answer":"14","solution":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 14."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Starting computation before identifying the required quantity.','Applying a memorized formula to the wrong relationship.','Dropping a negative sign, unit, exponent, or grouping symbol.','Accepting an answer without checking it against the original conditions.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Estimate before solving so unreasonable options are easier to eliminate.','Write one clean intermediate line for multi-step calculations.','Use answer choices strategically, but still verify the governing method.','Return to skipped hard items after securing faster questions.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"What is the median of 7, 12, 17, 22, 27?","answer":"17","explanation":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 17."},{"prompt":"What is the median of 8, 14, 20, 26, 32?","answer":"20","explanation":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 20."},{"prompt":"What is the median of 9, 16, 23, 30, 37?","answer":"23","explanation":"The values are ordered and the middle of five values is 23."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='statistics' and s.slug='mathematics';
update public.lessons l set overview='Count outcomes and model practical multi-step situations. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result.',objectives=array['Represent the given information accurately in probability and applied problems.','Select and apply the appropriate formula or property in probability and applied problems.','Show an efficient solution without skipping essential reasoning in probability and applied problems.','Check magnitude, sign, units, and reasonableness in probability and applied problems.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Count outcomes and model practical multi-step situations."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"Probability is favorable outcomes divided by all equally likely outcomes."},{"title":"CET application","body":"CET items usually combine the basic rule with an unfamiliar-looking expression, diagram, or word problem. The reliable approach is to translate the information, choose the governing relationship, solve carefully, and check the result."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Identify what is given and what must be found.','Rewrite the information using symbols, a table, or a labeled sketch.','Choose the property or formula that connects the known and unknown values.','Carry out one justified operation at a time and keep units consistent.','Substitute the result back or estimate to confirm that it is reasonable.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":null,"prompt":"A bag contains 2 red and 3 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"2/5","solution":"There are 2 favorable outcomes among 5 tokens, so the probability is 2/5."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":null,"prompt":"A bag contains 3 red and 4 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"3/7","solution":"There are 3 favorable outcomes among 7 tokens, so the probability is 3/7."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":null,"prompt":"A bag contains 4 red and 5 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"4/9","solution":"There are 4 favorable outcomes among 9 tokens, so the probability is 4/9."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Starting computation before identifying the required quantity.','Applying a memorized formula to the wrong relationship.','Dropping a negative sign, unit, exponent, or grouping symbol.','Accepting an answer without checking it against the original conditions.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Estimate before solving so unreasonable options are easier to eliminate.','Write one clean intermediate line for multi-step calculations.','Use answer choices strategically, but still verify the governing method.','Return to skipped hard items after securing faster questions.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"A bag contains 5 red and 6 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"5/11","explanation":"There are 5 favorable outcomes among 11 tokens, so the probability is 5/11."},{"prompt":"A bag contains 6 red and 7 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"6/13","explanation":"There are 6 favorable outcomes among 13 tokens, so the probability is 6/13."},{"prompt":"A bag contains 7 red and 8 blue tokens. What is the probability of drawing a red token at random?","answer":"7/15","explanation":"There are 7 favorable outcomes among 15 tokens, so the probability is 7/15."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='probability' and s.slug='mathematics';
update public.lessons l set overview='Connect cell structures with their functions. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

CET science questions reward connected understanding: identify the system, recall the governing principle, predict what changes, and distinguish evidence from assumption. Memorized terms help only when their functions and relationships are understood.',objectives=array['Define the major structures, quantities, or processes in cells and organelles.','Explain cause-and-effect relationships in cells and organelles.','Apply a scientific principle to a new situation in cells and organelles.','Interpret observations, variables, and evidence in cells and organelles.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Connect cell structures with their functions."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"Structure supports function at every biological level."},{"title":"CET application","body":"CET science questions reward connected understanding: identify the system, recall the governing principle, predict what changes, and distinguish evidence from assumption. Memorized terms help only when their functions and relationships are understood."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Name the branch and system involved.','List the relevant facts or variables from the question.','Recall the law, process, or structure–function relationship that governs the situation.','Predict the result while holding unrelated factors constant.','Check that the conclusion follows from evidence rather than an unsupported assumption.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":null,"prompt":"Which term means “stores most genetic material”?","answer":"nucleus","solution":"nucleus is stores most genetic material."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":null,"prompt":"Which term means “builds proteins”?","answer":"ribosome","solution":"ribosome is builds proteins."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":null,"prompt":"Which term means “releases usable energy from food”?","answer":"mitochondrion","solution":"mitochondrion is releases usable energy from food."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Confusing related terms that operate at different levels.','Treating correlation as proof of causation.','Ignoring a controlled variable or stated experimental condition.','Choosing an absolute claim when the evidence supports only a limited conclusion.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Sketch cycles, forces, circuits, or systems when relationships are hard to track.','Pay attention to words such as increase, decrease, constant, and most directly.','Eliminate choices that violate conservation, structure–function, or fair-test principles.','Use units and direction to check physics and chemistry calculations.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"Which term means “regulates movement into and out of the cell”?","answer":"cell membrane","explanation":"cell membrane is regulates movement into and out of the cell."},{"prompt":"Which term means “captures light energy for photosynthesis”?","answer":"chloroplast","explanation":"chloroplast is captures light energy for photosynthesis."},{"prompt":"Which term means “stores water and dissolved materials”?","answer":"vacuole","explanation":"vacuole is stores water and dissolved materials."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='cells' and s.slug='science';
