e all flood risk.","prompt":"What is the primary purpose of the passage?","answer":"to explain an observed result and its limitation or implication","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: Mangrove restoration can reduce erosion but is not complete flood protection."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":"A school replaced disposable cups with refill stations. Plastic waste fell, but water use rose slightly because the stations required daily cleaning.","prompt":"What is the primary purpose of the passage?","answer":"to explain an observed result and its limitation or implication","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: The refill program reduced plastic while creating a smaller water-use tradeoff."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Selecting a true statement that does not answer the question.','Using personal knowledge instead of passage evidence.','Treating one detail as the main idea of the entire passage.','Choosing extreme language when the author uses qualified language.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Return to the relevant lines instead of relying on memory.','Watch contrast signals such as however, although, and but.','For inference, choose what must or most reasonably follows.','Check axes, units, legends, and time periods in visual information.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"What is the primary purpose of the passage?","answer":"to explain an observed result and its limitation or implication","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: The better variety depends on the expected water conditions."},{"prompt":"What is the primary purpose of the passage?","answer":"to explain an observed result and its limitation or implication","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Protected lanes increased cycling without substantially delaying buses."},{"prompt":"What is the primary purpose of the passage?","answer":"to explain an observed result and its limitation or implication","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Spaced review improved recall in the described comparison."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='purpose-audience' and s.slug='reading-comprehension';
update public.lessons l set overview='Recognize comparison, cause-effect, sequence, and problem-solution. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

Reading questions are evidence tasks. A defensible answer must match the passage’s actual scope, wording, and purpose—not merely something that could be true outside the text.',objectives=array['State the central idea at the correct level of scope in text structure.','Locate evidence for explicit and inferred claims in text structure.','Analyze tone, purpose, structure, and context in text structure.','Synthesize prose with tables or a second text in text structure.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Recognize comparison, cause-effect, sequence, and problem-solution."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"Signal words reveal relationships among ideas."},{"title":"CET application","body":"Reading questions are evidence tasks. A defensible answer must match the passage’s actual scope, wording, and purpose—not merely something that could be true outside the text."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Preview the question so you know what evidence to track.','Read the passage for its claim, structure, and changes in direction.','Mark the sentence or data point that supports each possible answer.','Reject choices that are unsupported, too broad, too narrow, or reversed.','Restate the winning answer in your own words and compare it with the text.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":"A barangay library extended its hours during examination week. Attendance rose most on evenings when volunteer tutors were present. The librarian plans to keep two evening schedules each week.","prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: Evening access paired with tutoring increased library use."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":"Mangrove roots slow coastal water and trap sediment. Communities that restored mangroves recorded less erosion during ordinary storms, though the trees did not eliminate all flood risk.","prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: Mangrove restoration can reduce erosion but is not complete flood protection."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":"A school replaced disposable cups with refill stations. Plastic waste fell, but water use rose slightly because the stations required daily cleaning.","prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: The refill program reduced plastic while creating a smaller water-use tradeoff."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Selecting a true statement that does not answer the question.','Using personal knowledge instead of passage evidence.','Treating one detail as the main idea of the entire passage.','Choosing extreme language when the author uses qualified language.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Return to the relevant lines instead of relying on memory.','Watch contrast signals such as however, although, and but.','For inference, choose what must or most reasonably follows.','Check axes, units, legends, and time periods in visual information.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: The better variety depends on the expected water conditions."},{"prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Protected lanes increased cycling without substantially delaying buses."},{"prompt":"Which structure best describes the passage?","answer":"observation followed by result or response","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Spaced review improved recall in the described comparison."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='structure' and s.slug='reading-comprehension';
update public.lessons l set overview='Infer unfamiliar words from definitions, contrasts, and examples. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

Reading questions are evidence tasks. A defensible answer must match the passage’s actual scope, wording, and purpose—not merely something that could be true outside the text.',objectives=array['State the central idea at the correct level of scope in context clues.','Locate evidence for explicit and inferred claims in context clues.','Analyze tone, purpose, structure, and context in context clues.','Synthesize prose with tables or a second text in context clues.']::text[],concept_sections='[{"title":"Foundation","body":"Infer unfamiliar words from definitions, contrasts, and examples."},{"title":"Governing rule","body":"Replace the inferred meaning in the sentence to test it."},{"title":"CET application","body":"Reading questions are evidence tasks. A defensible answer must match the passage’s actual scope, wording, and purpose—not merely something that could be true outside the text."}]'::jsonb,method_steps=array['Preview the question so you know what evidence to track.','Read the passage for its claim, structure, and changes in direction.','Mark the sentence or data point that supports each possible answer.','Reject choices that are unsupported, too broad, too narrow, or reversed.','Restate the winning answer in your own words and compare it with the text.']::text[],worked_examples='[{"title":"Guided example 1","passage":"A barangay library extended its hours during examination week. Attendance rose most on evenings when volunteer tutors were present. The librarian plans to keep two evening schedules each week.","prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"Evening access paired with tutoring increased library use.","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: Evening access paired with tutoring increased library use."},{"title":"Guided example 2","passage":"Mangrove roots slow coastal water and trap sediment. Communities that restored mangroves recorded less erosion during ordinary storms, though the trees did not eliminate all flood risk.","prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"Mangrove restoration can reduce erosion but is not complete flood protection.","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: Mangrove restoration can reduce erosion but is not complete flood protection."},{"title":"Guided example 3","passage":"A school replaced disposable cups with refill stations. Plastic waste fell, but water use rose slightly because the stations required daily cleaning.","prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"The refill program reduced plastic while creating a smaller water-use tradeoff.","solution":"The answer stays within the evidence: The refill program reduced plastic while creating a smaller water-use tradeoff."}]'::jsonb,common_mistakes=array['Selecting a true statement that does not answer the question.','Using personal knowledge instead of passage evidence.','Treating one detail as the main idea of the entire passage.','Choosing extreme language when the author uses qualified language.']::text[],exam_tips=array['Return to the relevant lines instead of relying on memory.','Watch contrast signals such as however, although, and but.','For inference, choose what must or most reasonably follows.','Check axes, units, legends, and time periods in visual information.']::text[],quick_checks='[{"prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"The better variety depends on the expected water conditions.","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: The better variety depends on the expected water conditions."},{"prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"Protected lanes increased cycling without substantially delaying buses.","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Protected lanes increased cycling without substantially delaying buses."},{"prompt":"In context, which meaning best fits the key result described?","answer":"Spaced review improved recall in the described comparison.","explanation":"The answer stays within the evidence: Spaced review improved recall in the described comparison."}]'::jsonb,source_links='[{"title":"DepEd Strengthened Senior High School Program","url":"https://www.deped.gov.ph/strengthened-shs-program/"},{"title":"UPCAT official site","url":"https://upcat.up.edu.ph/"},{"title":"USTET official site","url":"https://ustet.ust.edu.ph/"}]'::jsonb,estimated_minutes=20,status='published' from public.topics t join public.subjects s on s.id=t.subject_id where l.topic_id=t.id and t.slug='context-clues' and s.slug='reading-comprehension';
update public.lessons l set overview='Combine compatible claims and note disagreement. This lesson moves from the underlying idea to a repeatable method, then applies it to CET-style examples. The goal is not just to remember an answer but to explain why the method works and when it applies.

